# Maleo environment reference.
#
# This is the ONLY env template in the repository. There are no package-local
# .env files — dev scripts load this one with `--env-file ../../.env`. See
# AGENTS.md, "Environment".
#
# Every line is commented out on purpose. `bun run setup` writes a working .env,
# verifies the installed local Inngest CLI, and runs database migrations.
# with sane defaults; copying this file wholesale would fill it with empty
# values that then override those defaults. Uncomment only what you need.
#
# Set the media backend explicitly. Provider credentials remain optional.
#
# Grouped by the service that reads each variable.

# ─── Runtime data (read everywhere) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to <repo>/data.
# MALEO_DATA_DIR=
# Postgres connection string. Required in production, where a host other than
# localhost must use sslmode=require or verify-full. Unset in development: an
# embedded Postgres starts under <data>/postgres on MALEO_PG_PORT.
# MALEO_DATABASE_URL=
# MALEO_PG_PORT=54329
# `bun run dev` starts local Inngest on :8288; no key or separate download is
# needed. Video Studio is available separately through `bun run video`.
# The pre-Postgres SQLite file, read only by `bun run db:migrate-from-sqlite`
# and the legacy maintenance scripts. Defaults to <data>/maleo.db.
# MALEO_DB_PATH=
# Storyboard versions kept per project beyond the ones that carry meaning
# (approved, rendered, referenced, artifact carriers). "off" keeps every version.
# MALEO_STORYBOARD_RETENTION_WINDOW=20

# ─── Durable media (API, media worker, video service) ─────────────────────────
# Choose "local" only for development. Production requires "s3".
# MALEO_MEDIA_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
# S3-compatible storage: RustFS, R2, or S3. Both endpoints target the same
# private bucket; PUBLIC_ENDPOINT must resolve from the operator's browser.
# MALEO_MEDIA_S3_BUCKET=
# MALEO_MEDIA_S3_ENDPOINT=
# MALEO_MEDIA_S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT=
# MALEO_MEDIA_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# MALEO_MEDIA_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# MALEO_MEDIA_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# MALEO_MEDIA_URL_LIFETIME_SECONDS=300
# Handed to external providers, which queue before fetching, so it outlives the
# browser lifetime above:
# MALEO_MEDIA_EXTERNAL_URL_LIFETIME_SECONDS=3600
# Self-hosted RustFS stack only (Coolify secrets, not application env). RustFS
# has one key pair: the application credentials above are also its admin
# credentials, so a leaked key reaches the whole store — see docs/self-hosting.md.
# MALEO_MEDIA_CORS_ORIGIN=https://app.example.com

# ─── apps/api — the HTTP API ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# MALEO_API_PORT=8090
# MALEO_API_URL=http://localhost:8090

# Generated media. Setting worker URL makes `bun run dev` start media worker and
# lets local Inngest discover its function endpoint.
# MALEO_GEN_WORKER_URL=
# MALEO_GEN_WORKER_PUBLIC_URL=
# MALEO_GEN_WORKER_TOKEN=
# MALEO_GENERATION_CONCURRENCY_PER_KIND=

# Speech
# MALEO_TTS_PROVIDER=
# MALEO_TTS_CANVAS_TIMEOUT_MS=

# Caption execution belongs to media worker. API uses worker URL/service token.
# MALEO_WHISPER_CPP_DIR=data/whisper.cpp
# MALEO_WHISPER_CPP_VERSION=1.5.5
# MALEO_WHISPER_MODEL=base
# MALEO_CAPTION_CACHE_DIR=data/caption-cache
# MALEO_CAPTION_TRANSCRIBE=0
# MALEO_WHISPER_AUTO_INSTALL=0

# Gemini Canvas and BrowserOS drive a real browser over CDP. They are
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY — a container has no browser, so a deployed image provider is
# Cloudflare Workers AI or Hugging Face below.
# Gemini Canvas provider (Chrome CDP — see `bun run gemini-canvas-chrome`)
# GEMINI_IMAGE_CANVAS_URL=
# GEMINI_TTS_CANVAS_URL=
# BROWSEROS_MCP_URL=

# Cloudflare Workers AI image provider (MALEO_PROVIDER_IMAGE=cloudflare-ai).
# Free allocation is 10,000 neurons/day, no card, resetting daily. Measured cost
# per image at the sizes this provider requests (flux-2-klein-4b):
#   1:1  1088x1088   13.4 neurons  -> 744/day
#   4:5  1088x1360   42.8 neurons  -> 233/day
#   3:4  1104x1472   57.3 neurons  -> 174/day
#   16:9 1792x1008   75.3 neurons  -> 132/day
#   9:16 1008x1792   75.3 neurons  -> 132/day
# Output at or below 1024x1024 is not billed at all. Both vars are required
# before the provider reports ready.
# MALEO_CF_ACCOUNT_ID=
# MALEO_CF_API_TOKEN=
# Model must be one this repo describes; an unknown id is a configuration error.
#   @cf/black-forest-labs/flux-2-klein-4b  (default) 256-1920px, 4 reference images
#   @cf/black-forest-labs/flux-1-schnell   cheaper, SQUARE ONLY, no references
# MALEO_CF_IMAGE_MODEL=

# Hugging Face Inference Providers image provider (MALEO_PROVIDER_IMAGE=huggingface).
# Reaches 200+ models through one router at pass-through provider pricing. This
# is a breadth path, not a free one: free accounts get $0.10/month of credits,
# roughly 30 flux-schnell images.
#
# TWO LIMITS, verified against the live API. Neither errors — this provider takes
# what the router gives it, so both fail SILENTLY by design:
#   - Reference images are ignored. The text-to-image task has no such parameter,
#     so references picked in the UI have no effect on the result.
#   - Requested aspect is often ignored. The serving providers behind the router
#     drop the documented width/height (nscale returns 1024x1024, fal-ai
#     1024x768), so a 9:16 request can come back square and still report success.
# Use cloudflare-ai when the aspect or the references have to be honoured.
# HF_TOKEN=
# HF_BILL_TO=
# MALEO_HF_IMAGE_MODEL=
# Pin a serving provider instead of the router's "auto" (e.g. fal-ai, nscale).
# The lever for the aspect limit above, if one is found that honours size.
# MALEO_HF_INFERENCE_PROVIDER=

# Scene extraction
# SCENE_EXTRACTOR_DISABLED=
# SCENE_EXTRACTOR_TIMEOUT_MS=

# Downstream services the API calls
# MALEO_VIDEO_URL=
# MALEO_VIDEO_TOKEN=

# Sound search
# FREESOUND_API_KEY=

# Notifications
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Threads publishing
# THREADS_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# THREADS_USER_ID=

# ─── Deployment only (see docs/self-hosting.md) ───────────────────────────────
# Not needed for `bun run dev`; each is REQUIRED in production, and the API
# refuses to start naming whichever is missing.
# MALEO_SERVICE_TOKEN=      # worker -> API /internal/* authentication
# MALEO_MASTER_KEY=         # wraps every stored provider credential
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=        # signs operator sessions
# MALEO_API_PUBLIC_URL=     # the API's own public origin
# MALEO_API_CORS_ORIGINS=   # origins allowed to carry a session — the web one
# INNGEST_BASE_URL=          # self-hosted server, or Inngest Cloud
# INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=
# INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=       # plain hex for the self-hosted server
# INNGEST_APP_ID=            # per function host; the media worker uses maleo-media

# ─── apps/web — the web client ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MALEO_WEB_PORT=3030

# ─── packages/media + apps/media-worker — generation worker ───────────────────
# MALEO_MEDIA_WORKER_PORT=
# GEN_WORKER_DB=
# CACHE_DIR=

# ─── apps/render-worker — Remotion render server ───────────────────────────────
# MALEO_VIDEO_PORT=
# MALEO_VIDEO_TOKEN=
# MALEO_VIDEO_DB=
# MALEO_VIDEO_CORS_ORIGINS=
# MALEO_VIDEO_CONCURRENCY=
# MALEO_VIDEO_LEASE_STALE_MS=
# MALEO_VIDEO_DEDUPE_WINDOW_MS=
# MALEO_VIDEO_JOB_RETENTION=
# Export authority (remotion|rust) and shadow comparison runs (off turns them off).
# MALEO_EXPORT_RENDERER=
# MALEO_EXPORT_SHADOW=
# MALEO_RENDER_HOST=
# Optional render-time scene-image repair service used only by packages/video.
# API image generation does not read these variables.
# MALEO_IMAGE_URL=
# MALEO_IMAGE_TOKEN=

# Media APIs used while rendering
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
# REMOVE_BG_API_KEY=

# Lambda rendering. AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY are read by the
# Remotion Lambda SDK rather than by our own code, so they appear in no grep of
# this repository — they are still required for a Lambda render.
# REMOTION_AWS_REGION=
# REMOTION_LAMBDA_FUNCTION=
# REMOTION_LAMBDA_SERVE_URL=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ─── packages/stock — stock media lookup ──────────────────────────────────────
# PEXELS_API_KEY=
# FREESOUND_LICENSE_FILTER=
# FREESOUND_COMMERCIAL_USE_APPROVED=no
# STOCK_MUSIC_HOST=
# STOCK_MUSIC_PREFIX=
# B2_KEY_ID=
# B2_APP_KEY=
# B2_BUCKET_NAME=

# ─── apps/api — Threads OAuth ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# THREADS_APP_ID=
# THREADS_APP_SECRET=
# THREADS_REDIRECT_URI=
